### Interpretations
1. [derived from Facts 1, 2, 3, 5, 7, 8, 9-11] Across the reviewed runs, Narrative frequently appears as the earliest observable stage that departs from the requested company-first editorial hierarchy.
2. [derived from Facts 1, 17, 19, 20] The report's documented recommendation is to treat Narrative as the controlled intervention point in a next trial that compares Synthesis inputs and then evaluates factual integrity, company-first hierarchy preservation, and editorial quality.

